# Resource storage must-do

## Placement reads that still load whole journals

Admission reads only in-flight intents (`readPlacementAdmissionView`, the
`state` and `operationId` indexes, a stored high-water counter). Two readers
still load every intent a handle ever stored:

- The reactive account projection and `commitPlan` read full per-handle
  journals. Receipts, Undo and identity checks read settled intents there
  (`intents[0].projectId`, a settled create, `settledAt`). Move those readers to
  on-demand journal reads, then trim the projection to unresolved intents.
- Folder records load whole for parent resolution because their intents are
  embedded in the record. Store folder intents beside the record, indexed like
  files.

Cost grows with a handle's lifetime of moves, so a long-lived chapter slows
every projection. A probe with 10, 1,000 and 10,000 settled intents on one
handle loads 10,001 intents through these readers
(`work/drag-anywhere/evidence/reorder-history-scan/` in the docs repo).
